From: Kestrel OS port <local>
Subject: [PATCH, DIAGNOSTIC, LOCAL-ONLY] disable display subsystem on Slim 3

Rationale: the mdss driver (initramfs module) binds ae00000 and
takes over the firmware framebuffer, but the panel never lights:
screen goes black-with-backlight and all later boot text is
invisible. Keep the console on simplefb until panel bring-up is
solved. NOT for publication or general ARM64 support.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
@@ -1778,3 +1778,12 @@
 &gpu { status = "disabled"; };
 &gmu { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/* DIAGNOSTIC 2026-10-16 (0013): disable the display subsystem. The
+ * mdss driver (from initramfs modules) binds the subsystem and takes
+ * over the firmware framebuffer, but the panel never lights, so the
+ * screen goes black-with-backlight and all later text is invisible.
+ * Keep the console on simplefb until panel bring-up is solved.
+ * Local-only, not for publication. */
+&mdss { status = "disabled"; };
